 she  intentionally misled investors and she  you know knew the machines weren't  working and she used machines from other  companies i think the jury is going to  think about all that and wonder whether  or not she did this intentionally or she  was just trying to promote her company  like lots of people do in silicon valley  all right now julie on the other side  how was the defense going to respond and  raise any kind of reasonable doubt to  try to win this case  it look their their defense basically  even though they called several  witnesses really relied on her she  testified it what was it seven or eight  days under cross examination  and at the end of the day she gave a  complicated a bit confusing a bit  inconsistent  level of testimony that in many ways  blamed her boyfriend at the time for his  uh for domestic violence towards her  that caused these all these things to  happen i think that's going to be a  problem i think the jury's not buying  that and i think the best thing they  have is what terry kind of talked about  is the idea is did she intentionally  defraud investors or did she use puffery  i mean that is kind of the the thing  that the jury's gonna have to decide and  i think if they push towards the  domestic violence the jury's not going  to buy any of it all right we'll see how  it plays out again we've just got more  closing arguments both for the defense  and prosecution and we'll give you  updates as we continue when we come back  a disgraced hollywood filmmaker's  lawyers work to get a sexual assault  conviction overturned the arguments  harvey weinstein's attorney is making to  appeal  welcome back to long crime daily  disgrace movie producer harvey weinstein  could have his conviction on sex crimes  charges in new york thrown out at a  hearing this week appeals court judges  question what they called prejudicial  evidence used to convict weinstein the  judge in the new york case allowed three  women to testify for the prosecution  about their claims that weinstein  assaulted them however weinstein was not  charged with assaulting those women law  and crime spoke with weinstein's  attorney in the new york case about the  conviction last summer  these are all women of  adult age all women who at least in my  case in new york and some of the l.a  witnesses who testified as other crimes  witnesses in new york all testified to  the fact that they wanted something from  harvey weinstein and so you know the  question becomes can we put all these  cases in the same box and i really don't  think that we can i will maintain um  until the end of my career or maybe  until my grave that they did not have  enough evidence to find harvey guilty in  that case and they did find him not  guilty of free of account so i mean  that's something that to think  about weinstein is in jail in los  angeles awaiting trial a judge refused  to dismiss his case last week  and one of the first of harvey  weinstein's accusers actress rose  mcgowan won't have her lawsuit case  against him heard in court which is  separate from the sexual assault  allegations this comes after was  dismissed by a california judge last  week the lawsuit accused weinstein and  his attorneys of trying to silence her  from coming forward with rape  allegations the judge says mccowan  missed the deadline to file paperwork in  her case her claims were dismissed with  prejudice meaning she can't refile the  same claim again in that court  julie the main issue in this appeals  case seems to be prejudicial evidence  what exactly is that and where's the  line for prosecutions when presenting  that in a case  look we saw this in bill cosby although  they overturned for different reasons i  mean the issue is whether or not the  judge allowed extrinsic evidence into  this case to such a degree that the  prejudicial value of that evidence  outweighed the probative meaning did the  jury basically find him guilty because  he's just a really bad guy based on this  